[{"answer":"It is good to be polite.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/1.mp3"},{"answer":"People like you more when you are polite.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/2.mp3"},{"answer":"Always say please and thank you.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/3.mp3"},{"answer":"If you ask for some milk, you should say,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/4.mp3"},{"answer":"\"Please, may I have a glass of milk?\"","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/5.mp3"},{"answer":"When someone gives you the milk, you should respond with \"Thank you\".","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/6.mp3"},{"answer":"It is not difficult to be polite.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/7.mp3"},{"answer":"You should not push or shove people.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/8.mp3"},{"answer":"You should cover your mouth when you cough or sneeze.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/9.mp3"},{"answer":"You should address people properly.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/10.mp3"},{"answer":"If you are trying to get someone's attention, you would say, \"excuse me\".","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/11.mp3"},{"answer":"You wouldn't say, \"hey you\".","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/12.mp3"},{"answer":"There are table manners.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/13.mp3"},{"answer":"That is where you eat properly and politely at the dinner table.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/14.mp3"},{"answer":"You don't shove food into your mouth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/15.mp3"},{"answer":"You don't reach over other people's plates.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/16.mp3"},{"answer":"You don't talk with your mouth full.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/17.mp3"},{"answer":"All of these things are common sense.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/18.mp3"},{"answer":"Being polite is mostly thinking about how you would like to be treated.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/19.mp3"},{"answer":"You wouldn't want people to be impolite to you.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/20.mp3"},{"answer":"It is not polite to point at people. It is not polite to burp out loud.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/21.mp3"},{"answer":"It is not polite to use someone else's things without asking first.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/22.mp3"},{"answer":"Being polite just comes naturally if you have been brought up in a home where everyone was polite.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/ielts-listening-62-2019-03-29-12-39-38/23.mp3"}]
